  <p style="letter-spacing:2px;font-size:0.8em;color:#c9a84c;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:8px;"><strong>The Aiper Pool Cleaner Lineup, Explained</strong></p>
  <h2 style="color:#232739;font-size:1.8em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:20px;">Cordless Robotic Pool Cleaning, Built to Match Your Pool</h2>

  <p>Pool cleaning has traditionally meant one of three things: a weekly service invoice, a pressure or suction cleaner permanently tethered to your filtration system, or an afternoon spent with a net and a brush. Aiper builds cordless robotic cleaners that remove all three from the equation. Drop one in, let it run its cycle, and lift it out when it's done, no hose to drag around the deck, no plumbing to tie into, and no recurring truck roll from a pool service.</p>

  <p>Aiper isn't a single machine, it's a lineup, and that matters because pools aren't all the same. A small above-ground pool and a 3,000-square-foot in-ground pool with a sloped floor and stairs don't need the same robot, and buying more machine than your pool requires is just money spent on capability you'll never use. Yard Automation Pros carries four active Aiper models, from the compact Scuba 800 up to the flagship Scuba X1 Pro Max, so the starting point is matching the robot to the pool, not the other way around.</p>

  <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0965/2056/9136/files/aiper_scuba_x1_pro_max_robotic_pool_cleaner_2_1000x_ef733371-cea4-43d5-b238-0e04b54969b1.jpg?v=1788708089" alt="Aiper Scuba X1 Pro Max cordless robotic pool cleaner" style="width:100%; border-radius:8px; margin: 24px 0;" loading="lazy" width="1000" height="1000">

  <h3 style="color:#232739;margin-top:36px;">What Every Aiper Cleaner Has in Common</h3>

  <p>Every model in the lineup shares the same basic premise: cordless operation, an internal rechargeable battery, onboard filtration that captures debris as it cleans, and app connectivity for starting cycles and checking status. None of them require a permanent connection to your pool's plumbing or filtration system, which means no professional installation, no impact on your pump's flow rate, and no cleaner competing with your filtration system for suction. You charge it, place it in the water, and it works independently until the cycle finishes or the battery runs low, at which point most models return themselves to a resting or docking position automatically.</p>

  <p>Where the lineup diverges is navigation intelligence, coverage area, which surfaces get cleaned, and battery runtime, and that's exactly the set of variables that should decide which model is right for a given pool.</p>

  <hr style="border:none;border-top:1px solid #e5e5e5;margin:48px 0 0;">
  <h3 style="color:#232739;margin-top:48px;">Scuba X1 Pro Max: The Flagship, for Large and Complex Pools</h3>

  <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0965/2056/9136/files/aiper_scuba_x1_pro_max_robotic_pool_cleaner_15_1800x_2e0a6e32-4fae-439e-b7be-95dc583972e6.jpg?v=1788708089" alt="Aiper Scuba X1 Pro Max cleaning pool floor" style="width:100%; border-radius:8px; margin: 20px 0;" loading="lazy" width="1800" height="1800">

  <p>The Scuba X1 Pro Max is built for pools where coverage and complexity are the real challenge, up to 3,230 square feet, up to 100 feet in length, with slopes, elevated platforms, and curved walls that would confuse a simpler cleaner. Nine motors and a TVC propulsion engine, the same category of thrust-vectoring design used in fighter jet control systems, give it the maneuverability to hold a line across an uneven floor instead of drifting or stalling out.</p>

  <p>FlexiPath™ 2.0 scans the pool in 3D and plans an adaptive route rather than running a fixed pattern, while OmniSense+™ 2.0 uses 24 ultrasonic sensors and a quad-core chip to map the pool's exact layout in real time and tailor the cleaning pattern to that specific shape. It's the only model in the lineup rated to clean the full envelope, floor, walls, waterline, slopes, elevated platforms, and the water surface, in a single machine. HomeComingDock™ returns it to the entry point automatically when a cycle ends, so there's no wading in or fishing it out with a pole, and HydroComm Pure connectivity lets you monitor battery, switch modes, and trigger one-tap retrieval from your phone even while it's working underwater.</p>

  <p>At 8,500 GPH suction, up to 300 minutes of floor-cleaning runtime (600 minutes in surface-only mode), and dual filtration down to a 3-micron MicroMesh™ ultra-fine filter, it's built for owners who want one machine to handle everything a large, architecturally complex pool can throw at it.</p>

  <h3 style="color:#232739;margin-top:40px;">Scuba N3: Cognitive AI, Trained on Real Pool Data</h3>

  <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0965/2056/9136/files/ScubaN3CognitiveAIRoboticPoolCleaner_13_1800x_bc23bdfb-0b8b-4305-9f40-5b08cce30453.jpg?v=1788708219" alt="Aiper Scuba N3 cleaning pool with AI navigation" style="width:100%; border-radius:8px; margin: 20px 0;" loading="lazy" width="1800" height="1800">

  <p>The Scuba N3 is built around a genuinely different idea: instead of following a mapped route, its Cognitive AI Navium™ Mode was trained on real cleaning data gathered from more than 200 pools over two years of development, and it uses that training to adapt to your pool's exact layout in real time. AI Patrol Cleaning with VisionPath™ actively detects and targets debris as it finds it rather than waiting for it to be in the path of a fixed pattern, backed by dual brushes and 4,800 GPH suction for real pickup power once it gets there.</p>

  <p>JetAssist™ horizontal waterline cleaning handles the scum and mineral staining that collects right at the surface line, consistently the spot handheld cleaning misses most. The N3's construction is intentionally featherlight, making it easy to lower into the pool and lift back out without wrestling a heavy unit up over the coping. One click starts a cycle, and when it finishes, it returns to the waterline on its own and sends an alert to your phone. TÜV-certified data privacy protection keeps all AI processing on the device itself, so your pool's mapped layout data never leaves the machine.</p>

  <p>Rated for in-ground pools up to 1,600 square feet, cleaning floor, walls, waterline, and stairs, with up to 180 minutes of runtime.</p>

  <h3 style="color:#232739;margin-top:40px;">Scuba N1 Plus: Dependable Coverage, No Mapping Complexity</h3>

  <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0965/2056/9136/files/AiperScubaN1PlusRoboticPoolCleaner_2_1800x_c2a206e6-8a20-4b6e-8143-8f0b6dba4393.jpg?v=1789705217" alt="Aiper Scuba N1 Plus climbing pool wall" style="width:100%; border-radius:8px; margin: 20px 0;" loading="lazy" width="1800" height="1800">

  <p>Not every pool owner needs 3D mapping and AI-trained navigation, some just want a robot that reliably covers the floor, walls, and waterline every time it runs, without extra complexity to think about. The Scuba N1 Plus is built for exactly that: a brushless drain motor filtering up to 4,800 GPH, a dynamic silicone brush to lift dirt and debris, and caterpillar treads that give it strong surface contact for traction climbing from floor to wall.</p>

  <p>WavePath™ navigation reads the pool's natural water flow to increase coverage over time rather than repeating an identical route every run. Four selectable modes, Floor, Wall, Auto (floor plus wall plus waterline), and Eco, cover the range from a single targeted clean to a low-maintenance 45-minute cycle every 48 hours that keeps the pool consistently swim-ready without you scheduling anything. OTA updates through the Aiper app keep it current automatically, the same way a phone updates itself.</p>

  <p>Rated for in-ground pools up to 1,600 square feet and 50 feet in length, with up to 180 minutes of runtime and a 2-year manufacturer's warranty.</p>

  <h3 style="color:#232739;margin-top:40px;">Scuba 800: Compact and Simple, for Smaller Pools</h3>

  <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0965/2056/9136/files/2_1800x_c0f4ed3a-2338-44e4-95fa-098af1a41040.png?v=1789704017" alt="Aiper Scuba 800 hydrodynamic design in pool" style="width:100%; border-radius:8px; margin: 20px 0;" loading="lazy" width="1800" height="1800">

  <p>For above-ground and flat-floor pools up to 860 square feet, the Scuba 800 is the simplest entry point into the lineup, and simple is the point. A hydrodynamic body shape lets it move through the water efficiently, putting more of its power into cleaning instead of fighting drag, while dual-drive motors filter up to 1,320 GPH into a 2-liter filter box. An audio alert system tells you battery and cleaning status without needing to open an app, and when the cycle ends or the battery runs low, it auto-parks itself near the pool wall so it's easy to find and retrieve.</p>

  <p>A quick-drainage system releases up to 80% of the water it's holding in just 15 seconds before you lift it out, which sounds minor until you've hauled a soaked pool robot up a ladder without one. At 3.4kg, it's the lightest machine in the lineup and the easiest to store between uses.</p>

