  <h3 style="color:#232739;margin-top:40px;">Cordless Robotic vs. Corded Cleaners and Manual Cleaning</h3>

  <p>Older robotic pool cleaners plug into a wall outlet and drag a long floating power cord behind them in the water, a cord that can tangle on ladders, steps, and pool furniture, and that limits how far the robot can travel from the outlet. Pressure and suction cleaners tie directly into your pool's plumbing, adding a mechanical load to your filtration system and a hose that needs disconnecting and storing when not in use. Aiper's entire lineup skips both problems by running on an internal battery.</p>

