  <h3 style="color:#232739;margin-top:40px;">Maintenance and Filters</h3>

  <p>Every Aiper model uses replaceable, washable filtration, either a standard fine filter basket or an ultra-fine MicroMesh™ filter for finer debris like pollen and algae, and rinsing or swapping the filter after a cleaning cycle is the extent of regular upkeep. There's no motor oil, no belt, and no plumbing to maintain since the entire system is self-contained inside the robot. Manufacturer warranty coverage ranges from 1 year on the Scuba 800 up to 3 years on the Scuba X1 Pro Max, reflecting the difference in build complexity between the compact and flagship models.</p>

  <hr style="border:none;border-top:1px solid #e5e5e5;margin:48px 0 0;">
  <h3 style="color:#232739;margin-top:48px;">Common Questions About the Aiper Lineup</h3>

  <p><strong>Do I need to install anything or connect it to my pool's plumbing?</strong><br>
  No. Every Aiper model is fully cordless and self-contained. Charge it, place it in the water, and it cleans independently, no connection to your filtration system or pump required.</p>

  <p><strong>Will it work in an above-ground pool?</strong><br>
  Yes, the Scuba 800 is built specifically for above-ground and flat-floor pools. The larger models are designed primarily for in-ground pools with more complex geometry.</p>

  <p><strong>How do I know which model covers my pool size?</strong><br>
  Compare your pool's square footage against the coverage figures in the table above, the Scuba X1 Pro Max scales up to 3,230 sq ft while the Scuba 800 is built for pools up to 860 sq ft. When in doubt, size up rather than down.</p>

  <p><strong>Does it clean the waterline, or just the floor?</strong><br>
  It depends on the model. The Scuba X1 Pro Max, Scuba N3, and Scuba N1 Plus all clean the waterline in addition to the floor and walls. The Scuba 800 is a floor-only cleaner.</p>

  <p><strong>How long does the battery last per cleaning cycle?</strong><br>
  Runtime ranges from 90 minutes on the Scuba 800 up to 300 minutes (600 in surface-only mode) on the Scuba X1 Pro Max. Most residential pools are fully covered well within a single charge cycle.</p>

  <p><strong>What's the warranty?</strong><br>
  Coverage varies by model, from 1 year on the Scuba 800 up to 3 years on the flagship Scuba X1 Pro Max. Exact terms are listed in each product's specifications.</p>

  <p><strong>Can I finance an Aiper cleaner?</strong><br>
  Yes, financing is available at checkout through Shop Pay Installments across the Aiper lineup.</p>

  <h3 style="color:#232739;margin-top:40px;">Ownership, Handled</h3>

  <p>Every Aiper cleaner is typically delivered in about two weeks. Financing is available at checkout through Shop Pay Installments, so the cost spreads over time instead of landing as one lump sum. And you're not buying this from a manufacturer's storefront with no one to call, Yard Automation Pros provides real, US-based expert guidance before and after your purchase, from matching the right model to your pool to helping you get the most out of it once it's running. If something isn't working the way it should, you have a real person to reach, not a support ticket queue.</p>

